 "packet_verdict": "Packet 6c52f2cfd rejected: on held-out AW case surrogate_high_class (Java exit 0, normal class diagram) the tip exits 1 with the new export error from 61f3883ffb0f41be652951f257fb1eaa57dbf16d. That is a whole-output failure the packet causes on a fresh held-out case.",
 "findings": [
  "Theme list exact: Java src/main/resources/themes has 44 puml-theme-*.puml files; Rust get_theme_source embeds 35; the set difference is exactly amiga, blueprint, carbon-gray, crt-amber, crt-green, mimeograph, mono, plain, sunlust = JAVA_BUNDLED_UNSHIPPED_THEMES. ThemeUtils.loadTheme with from == null calls loadBundledOrLocalTheme, which reads the jar resource first, so these nine always load in Java. Jar lookup is case-sensitive, and Rust's case-sensitive contains() agrees ('!theme Plain' no longer gets the marker, whereas base emulated plain).",
  "The marker applies after TIM substitution (EaterTheme.analyze -> applyFunctionsAndVariables): AW theme_plain_variable now reaches the plain emulation (bytes change; difference count 15 in base and tip). Inactive !if branches emit no marker: AW theme_mono_inactive strict-matches in the tip (base DIFF 1).",
  "Theme failures are not caused by the packet: 6 of 9 AW theme outputs are byte-identical to base. All 9 except theme_mono_inactive fail strict compare in every tree because renderer emulation of unshipped themes is incomplete (pre-existing). theme_plain_then_cerulean: base DIFF 9, previous tip DIFF 23, tip DIFF 9. Round 2 removes the previous tip's regression. theme_mono_usecase also fails on diagram-type dispatch (Rust SEQUENCE vs Java DESCRIPTION) with or without any theme, in base and tip.",
  "Other forms (Rust-only, theme-probes.json): unknown names and shipped names are unchanged; 'from <dir>' reads puml-theme-NAME.puml as ThemeUtils.loadFileTheme does (local file applied); a missing theme still renders normally where Java raises 'Cannot load theme' / 'No such theme' (pre-existing error-contract gap). A local-file theme named 'plain' also triggers the plain renderer emulation; this is inherited from the previous tip (byte-identical) and not Java's behaviour, because Java executes only the local body.",
  "preproc_complex_theme_override: the gain is genuine. Base differs only in linearGradient ids; the tip emits Java's ids (seed over the expanded source). The previous tip and tip are byte-identical, and the round-2 marker cannot reach a shipped theme.",
  "Raw-reader record (T14.24): blank0/1/3 and raw_* AU pairs keep their round-1 results. raw_blank_before_start and raw_multi_blank_first_block remain T14.26 (pre-existing, out of scope). The record cannot be accepted while its fresh unshipped-theme pairs fail whole-output, and the packet is rejected."
 ],
 "bounded_next_obligations": [
  "Track renderer emulation of the nine unshipped Java themes as its own target, or ship equivalent theme bodies under a compatible licence, with the 8 failing AW theme_* pairs as acceptance.",
